{"key": ["adverse", 11, 31], "text": "**Step 1 CAUSE GATE:**\n- temp regime_z = -62.29\n- temp consistency_z = 15.88\n\nBoth the temp regime_z and temp consistency_z are significantly elevated well beyond the ordinary noise level (~1). This indicates a genuine sensor fault rather than benign flight-class variation.\n\n**Step 2 DIRECTION:**\n- temp regime_z is strongly negative (-62.29), indicating that temperatures are biased low. This suggests that the engine looks healthier than it actually is, making the model over-optimistic and its RUL estimate inflated.\n\n**Step 3 CORRECTION:**\n- The RUL history shows a large sustained jump from 44 to 64 cycles. This marks the onset of the shift. Extrapolating the pre-jump level (44 cycles) downward at 1/cycle per cycle, the true RUL at cycle 31 is estimated as 44 - 7 = 37 cycles.\n- Given the adverse shift and the elevated mc_std (4.81), further downward correction is warranted. A reasonable estimate of the true RUL is around 30 cycles.\n- Corrected RUL: 30 cycles (clipped to [0, 65]).\n\n**Step 4 DECIDE:**\n- Corrected RUL of 30 cycles is greater than 10 but less than 25. Given the confirmed adverse shift, an inspection is warranted even though the corrected RUL is not extremely short.\n\n**FINAL:**\n```json\n{\n  \"shift_detected\": true,\n  \"shift_direction\": \"adverse\",\n  \"reliability\": \"low\",\n  \"corrected_rul\": 30,\n  \"decision\": \"inspect\",\n  \"confidence\": 0.9,\n  \"reasoning\": \"The sensor measurements indicate a genuine fault, leading to an over-optimistic RUL estimate.\"\n}\n```", "parsed": {"shift_detected": true, "shift_direction": "adverse", "reliability": "low", "corrected_rul": 30, "decision": "inspect", "confidence": 0.9, "reasoning": "The sensor measurements indicate a genuine fault, leading to an over-optimistic RUL estimate."}}
